        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="44" value="Invariant and why overlapping calls cannot break it" style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=21;fontColor=#152b46;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="58" y="1392" width="1684" height="33.35" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="45" value="For every workshop w: 0 &lt;= count(reservations for w) &lt;= w.capacity; UNIQUE(workshopId, studentId) enforces one seat per student.&#10;Every reservation writer first locks the same workshop row; a competitor waits until COMMIT/ROLLBACK, then later READ COMMITTED queries see committed seats.&#10;While holding that lock, check existing BEFORE full, then insert only if count &lt; capacity. Thus each new seat increases the count by exactly 1 within the limit.&#10;Capacity is immutable in this create/publish-only pilot. Database PKs, FKs, nonempty-title and capacity CHECK constraints support the invariant." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=19;fontColor=#152b46;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="58" y="1428" width="1684" height="107.60000000000001" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="46" value="Legend: blue = owned element; grey = external/supporting element; green = persistent store.&#10;Dashed boundary = named parent/scope. Arrow = labelled call/dependency; returns follow the call unless dashed.&#10;Arrows = labelled calls, type use or implementation. PK = primary key; FK = foreign key; Tx = transaction. Existing rows remain unchanged." style="text;html=0;whiteSpace=nowrap;overflow=visible;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=16;fontColor=#152b46;fontStyle=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry as="geometry" x="45" y="1575" width="1710" height="69.80000000000001" />
        </mxCell>
